# Supabase endpoint for the WordPress plugin build, loaded by Vite because
# `build:plugin` runs in mode=plugin.
#
# The publishable key is committed on purpose. It is not a credential: it
# identifies the project, it is meant to ship in client bundles, and it grants
# nothing on its own. Every table has RLS enabled and the anon policies are
# SELECT only, so the most anyone can do with this key is read the same rows the
# page already displays. Rotating it would be a code change, not a leak
# response.
#
# Baking it in is what makes the plugin upload-once. The alternative was having
# PHP print a window.jceConfig global, which means the plugin only reads
# Supabase if a piece of PHP that does not exist in this repo happens to be
# installed and correctly named -- otherwise the shipped plugin silently falls
# back to bundled data and nobody finds out until the news goes stale on the
# live site. With the endpoint in the bundle, uploading the zip once is enough:
# new stories, new polls and new seats then arrive from Supabase with no
# re-upload, because only the database changed, not the code.
#
# window.jceConfig still overrides both values at runtime if a site prefers to
# configure PHP, so this is a default rather than a commitment.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xbpimnerxjpwqnicwpec.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_LG2eHM6wdkMQYHUGTE0Xtg_VUxP4KGp
VITE_CYCLE=2026
